{"segment_id":"R10-003","code":"prompt-file-scope-narrowing","aspect":"context","quote":"Files named as 'the only files that matter':","memo":"Six-file list scopes the audit; libs/ signals sit outside it, and the broken surface later assessed never enters scope. locus: prompt","proposed_definition":"Prompt's 'only files that matter' list narrows what the agent audits."}
{"segment_id":"R10-003","code":"dead-code-flagged","aspect":"context","quote":"`//        url: chrome.extension.getURL('modules/charts/views/category.json'),`","memo":"Ground-truth lines 222 (and mainpage 46/58) are commented out; still listed as required changes. locus: harness","proposed_definition":"Harness ground-truth lists deprecated API lines that are commented out, with no live MV2 call present."}
{"segment_id":"R10-003","code":"flagged-unused-vendor-eval","aspect":"context","quote":"`libs/sb_admin_2_libs/bower_components/datatables-plugins/integration/bootstrap/2/index.html:11`","memo":"Remote-script signals hit bower demo HTML nothing loads, plus d3 library Function use. locus: harness","proposed_definition":"Migration signals flag eval/remote code in vendor or demo files regardless of whether shipped surfaces load them."}
{"segment_id":"R10-008","code":"background-to-service-worker","aspect":"action","quote":"\"background.scripts` (array) to `background.service_worker` (string)","memo":"Agent converts manifest background key to a service worker pointing at main.js.","proposed_definition":"Manifest background.page/persistent replaced by a service_worker entry."}
{"segment_id":"R10-009","code":"mv2-manifest-edit-success","aspect":"effect","quote":"Successfully replaced 3 block(s) in /work/run/out/manifest.json.","memo":"Manifest edit lands; but no check that main.js is service-worker-safe (uses chrome.tabs only, likely fine, yet untested).","proposed_definition":"edit tool reports successful replacement of the manifest blocks."}
{"segment_id":"R10-016","code":"edit-exact-match-failure","aspect":"effect","quote":"Could not find the exact text in /work/run/out/modules/charts/views/graph_of_visited_urls_and_referers.js.","memo":"First edit misses on whitespace; agent re-greps and retries. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"edit call fails exact-text match; agent re-greps or re-reads and retries."}
{"segment_id":"R10-017","code":"tool-error-flag","aspect":"effect","quote":"The old text must match exactly including all whitespace and newlines.","memo":"Tool error is a genuine mismatch, not a false alarm.","proposed_definition":"Tool reported an error requiring inspection of the exit/cause."}
{"segment_id":"R10-019","code":"grep-tool-false-match-suspect","aspect":"effect","quote":"No matches found","memo":"grep for the full quoted pattern returns nothing while the bare-pattern grep (R10-021) matches line 222 — quoted-pattern handling suspect. locus: environment","proposed_definition":"Grep returns no match for a pattern that demonstrably exists in the file, misleading the agent."}
{"segment_id":"R10-022","code":"edit-exact-match-failure","aspect":"action","quote":"Let's try to use a smaller `oldText`.","memo":"Agent shrinks oldText after the failed match and the retry succeeds.","proposed_definition":"Agent recovers from an edit mismatch by shortening or adjusting the match text."}
{"segment_id":"R10-023","code":"edit-dead-code-only","aspect":"action","quote":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /work/run/out/modules/charts/views/graph_of_visited_urls_and_referers.js.","memo":"Edited line 222 is commented out; no runtime behaviour changes despite successful edit. locus: harness","proposed_definition":"Agent edits commented-out lines as if they were live code, changing no runtime behaviour."}
{"segment_id":"R10-034","code":"edit-dead-code-only","aspect":"action","quote":"(this one is commented out, but the prompt says to change it)","memo":"Agent knowingly swaps getURL inside commented lines 46/58 of mainpage.js; cosmetic compliance with ground truth.","proposed_definition":"Agent edits commented-out lines as if they were live code, changing no runtime behaviour."}
{"segment_id":"R10-036","code":"usage-scoping-check","aspect":"action","quote":"let me see if these HTML files are actually used by the extension.","memo":"Agent checks whether flagged remote-script demo files are loaded before editing them.","proposed_definition":"Agent checks whether flagged or suspected files are actually loaded by shipped surfaces before editing them."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"untested-assumption","aspect":"intent","quote":"this specific line is part of a internal utility that may not be reached by the extension's specific usage","memo":"Agent assumes d3's new Function path is unreached with no evidence, under no-verification rule; leaves it in place. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent asserts runtime behaviour it cannot verify under the prompt's no-verification rule."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"considered-then-dropped","aspect":"intent","quote":"it would require a library update or a sandbox implementation.","memo":"Agent names the sandbox/bundle remedies for d3's Function call then performs neither edit.","proposed_definition":"Agent proposes a concrete edit then abandons it without acting."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"completion-claim-vs-evidence","aspect":"intent","quote":"The extension is now configured as an MV3 extension and is ready for loading.","memo":"Ready claim rests only on mechanical swaps; no load test possible, and outcome later shows toolbar_action=broken. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent declares migration complete while viewed evidence contradicts it."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"signals-miss-shipped-eval","aspect":"intent","quote":"The remote scripts are in ... these files are not referenced in the `manifest.json`","memo":"Agent reasons demo files are unused but never states whether d3.js itself is loaded by shipped pages, nor verifies d3 loading chain. ambiguous. locus: agent","proposed_definition":"Agent's usage scoping stays partial; whether the flagged library file is loaded is never resolved."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"verification-gap-never-tested","aspect":"effect","quote":"outcome: not_working score=0 | toolbar_action=broken","memo":"Header outcome names toolbar broken; transcript contains no reasoning about why the action would fail and no harness feedback arrived.","proposed_definition":"Packet outcome names broken or untestable surfaces the agent never checked and was never told about."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"run-ends-no-harness-feedback","aspect":"context","quote":"0 harness feedback msgs","memo":"Run closes on the agent's completion reply with zero repair rounds, unlike R01/R17.","proposed_definition":"Run ends on the agent's stop with no harness feedback message returned."}
{"segment_id":"R10-038","code":"no-verification-observed","aspect":"context","quote":"If the extension fails at runtime due to this, it would require a library update","memo":"Agent accepts possible runtime failure rather than self-checking, consistent with the prompt ban (R10-003 boilerplate).","proposed_definition":"Agent defers to the no-verification rule instead of self-checking a suspected runtime hazard."}
